From 687472671331ede03d7e4a77707e748e94351d4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:45:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] libretro: keep the address space across deinit

On Linux and macOS the emulator is only initialized once, but deinit
still released its address space and init reserved a new one. The SH4
context lives there and the CPU executors cache a pointer to it on init,
so a frontend that keeps the core loaded (Kodi does, and GNU unique
symbols keep it loaded anyway) loaded its next game against freed
memory: Verify Failed: !ctx->CpuRunning in Sh4Interpreter::Reset, or a
crash, whenever the new reservation landed somewhere else.

Keep the address space for as long as the emulator itself.
---
 shell/libretro/libretro.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp b/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp
index a4444c9..4f19717 100644
--- a/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -435,9 +435,9 @@ void retro_deinit()
 	}
 	os_UninstallFaultHandler();
 	
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || (defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__))
-	addrspace::release();
-#else
+	// Where the emulator is only initialized once (see retro_init), it also keeps
+	// its address space: the SH4 context lives there and is cached on init
+#if !defined(__APPLE__) && !(defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__))
 	emu.term();
 #endif
 	libretro_supports_bitmasks = false;
-- 
